# gnome-autoar -- archive integration for GNOME, and it is in this tree for
# exactly one consumer.
#
# gnome-shell's extensions tool takes it as a HARD dependency:
#
#     subprojects/extensions-tool/meson.build:32
#         autoar_dep = dependency('gnome-autoar-0')
#
# with no required:false, gated only on -Dextensions_tool, WHICH DEFAULTS TRUE.
# That dependency is invisible from gnome-shell's top-level meson.build -- it
# lives in a subproject, and gnome-shell ships its subprojects/ POPULATED rather
# than as bare wrap stubs, so nothing about the source tree announces that there
# is a second requirement surface inside it.
#
# The alternative was -Dextensions_tool=false. That was rejected: the extensions
# tool is how extensions are installed and managed, and turning off a deliverable
# to avoid packaging a small glib+libarchive library is not a trade.
#
# BLFS 12.4 pins 0.4.5, which is also the newest release; the book was checked
# rather than the directory listing, per the README Versions policy.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/gnome-autoar/0.4/gnome-autoar-0.4.5.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=838c5306fc38bfaa2f23abe24262f4bf15771e3303fb5dcb74f5b9c7a615dabe
SRC_DIR=gnome-autoar-0.4.5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -Dgtk=true, BECAUSE -Dgtk=false DOES NOT DISABLE GTK. IT IS A PROBE, NOT A
# SWITCH, AND THE BUILD PROVED IT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This recipe first shipped -Dgtk=false, to keep a GTK 3 edge out of a package
# that sits in GNOME_PKGS. CI failed on this package's OWN assertion, with the
# configure log reading `Run-time dependency gtk+-3.0 found: YES 3.24.50` -- the
# flag was set and the widgets were built anyway.
#
# The mechanism, from meson_options.txt:1 and meson.build:94-101:
#
#     option('gtk', type: 'boolean', value: true, ...)
#
#     gtk_dep = dependency('gtk+-3.0', version: '>= 3.2',
#                          required: get_option('gtk'), ...)
#     enable_gtk = gtk_dep.found()
#
# The option is a BOOLEAN, so it reaches `required:` as a bool -- and in meson,
# `required: false` means DO NOT FAIL IF MISSING. It does not mean do not look.
# The search still runs; GTK 3 is present in the seeded build image, so it is
# found; and enable_gtk is computed from .found() rather than from the option.
#
# SO THE OPTION CONTROLS WHETHER ABSENCE IS FATAL, AND NEVER WHETHER THE FEATURE
# IS BUILT. Only a meson `feature` option set to 'disabled' skips the lookup, and
# this one is not a feature. There is no way to decline the widgets short of
# patching, which is not worth it for two small files.
#
# Same family as gtk4's `if dependency(...).found()` false probe: a call that
# reads like a question about intent and is a question about the environment.
#
# THE CONSEQUENCE IS AN ORDERING ONE, and it is why this package moved lists.
# GTK 3 lives in NETWORK_UI_PKGS, so gnome-autoar cannot sit in GNOME_PKGS with
# a real gtk3 edge -- check-build-order rejects a package needing something from
# a later group. It is now in GNOME_UI_PKGS, after gtk3, which costs nothing:
# its only consumer is gnome-shell, which is later still.
#
# What is actually built by this is a SECOND library --
# gnome-autoar/meson.build:107-145 produces libgnome-autoar-gtk-0 with its own
# .pc -- of common GTK widgets. extensions-tool asks only for gnome-autoar-0.
# The widgets are unused here; they are accepted rather than chosen.
#
# -Dintrospection=enabled: the default is the FEATURE value 'auto', which finds
# gobject-introspection here and quietly succeeds. Pinned so it is a decision
# rather than a property of what happens to be installed -- the same reason the
# GIMP plugin is pinned off in libjxl. An 'auto' that gives the wanted answer
# today is not a recorded choice, and this one would silently drop the typelib if
# the build image ever changed underneath it.
#
# NOT SET, deliberately:
#
#   -Dvapi       already false, and self-guarding: meson.build:106 asserts that
#                introspection is enabled whenever vapi is.
#   -Dtests      already false upstream, unusually -- most of this tree's
#                packages have to turn tests off, this one ships them off.
#   -Dgtk_doc    already false, and it asserts -Dgtk when enabled, so it could
#                not be turned on here without reversing the decision above.
MESON_ARGS="-Dgtk=true -Dintrospection=enabled"
